  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Cooler than normal to start the workweek, then\nwarming trend.\n\nExpect high pressure over the Midwest to east/southeast into \nthe area through Tuesday. This will bring lower humidity and a \nbreeze today with temperatures running about 5-10 degrees below \nnormal.\n\nAs the high moves offshore by Wednesday should see temps\nreturning to at or above normal with increasing humidity.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Frontal boundary may bring some strong/severe\nstorms Thursday.\n\nDry through Wednesday, then an upper shortwave trough will \npivot across the Lower Great Lakes/Northeast Thursday, with a \nstrong southwesterly jet streak forecast to overspread parts of \nthe Ohio Valley into New England. A moist and unstable airmass \nis expected ahead of an eastward-advancing cold front and a \nsevere risk may unfold across parts of our area, but especially\nnorth of I-64. \n\nBeyond Thursday, models differ somewhat on speed of front and\nchance of showers/storms. Leaning toward slower solution, but by\nthe weekend its looking dry with another drop in humidity by\nSaturday.",
